  {
   "id": "nvidia-ceo-exit",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "Nvidia's chief resigns; Korean chip stocks and Nasdaq slip into its results",
   "when": "Thu 12 Nov · US evening",
   "what": "Nvidia said Jensen Huang stepped down as chief executive and as a director, effective immediately. CFO Colette Kress is interim chief while a search runs, and Harvey Jones became board chair. CNBC reports the shares fell 4.34% on Thursday, after sliding more intraday. On Friday KOSPI closed down 0.98% at 5,290.53 after opening up 2%. SK hynix fell 3.03% and Samsung Electronics 0.96%. Foreign investors sold a net 550.5 billion won. Nasdaq fell 0.91%. Nvidia reports on Tuesday 17 Nov.",
   "why": "Your Korea holdings (about 16.6% of the portfolio) lean on Samsung and SK hynix, whose fortunes follow AI chip demand. The tech funds and Nvidia share the same worry: who leads the company and what it says on Tuesday. Your Korea fund is priced at its 12 Nov NAV this morning, so Friday's fall is not yet in it.",
   "dir": "neg",
   "impact": 3,
