   "id": "fed-december-hike-bets",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Traders now fully price a December Fed hike as yields climb",
   "when": "Sun 15 Nov",
   "what": "CNBC says futures fully price a quarter-point Fed increase at the December meeting, with a small chance of a half-point move. The Fed raised rates in September to 3.75%-4.00% and held in October. Kansas City Fed president Jeff Schmid said inflation is uncomfortably above 2% and the Fed has more work to do. He is not a voter this year. The 10-year yield ended Friday near 5.15%, up about 29 basis points on the week. The S&P 500 fell 0.40% on Friday to 7,561.67.",
   "why": "About 25% of your portfolio is in US equities, mostly through S&P 500 funds. Higher yields tend to pressure share valuations, and a stronger dollar can shift the baht value of USD holdings. The Fed decision is on 9 Dec.",
