   "what": "CoinDesk says bitcoin is heading for a sixth straight weekly decline, down 11% in November and 21% this year. It links the weakness to money possibly being freed for the Anthropic share sale, Huang's exit and December rate-hike bets. CNBC says Anthropic is expected to price in a $70 to $78 range and start trading this Thursday. Bitcoin is about $65,100 this morning, up 1.55% in 24 hours.",
